  "description": "VESVUM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C198 H264 Ce6 N6 O30,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),C6 H14. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.555-4.694 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.51-164.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C198H264Ce6N6O30·4(C3H7NO)·C6H14. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ2-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV).",
